'''Coins''' {{Currency|Coin}} are a form of currency used to buy items in the [[shop]] such as [[boxes]], [[effects]], and [[pets]]. Coins spawn on the map for players to collect. The maximum amount that can be collected each round is 40. However, players that have purchased the [[Elite Gamepass]] can collect up to 50 coins.                                                                                                                                                                 

== Trivia ==
* The image for the old Coin {{Currency|Old Coin}} has reappeared in post-Season 1 events in the Token/Candy Exchange, despite being replaced by its new counterpart icon {{Currency|Coin}}.

* These were not the original form of currency. The original form of currency were called [[Points]], which could not be collected in game.

* Players were only allowed up to a maximum of 10 to 15 Coins {{Currency|Old Coin}} per round prior to the [[Season 1]] update. Many prices in the shop, like box prices, were lower due to the amount of coins that were possible to get (with the exception of some boxes being removed, like the [[Legendary Box]]).
** In hardcore, coins are gray.
*In the early stages of [[Murder Mystery 2]], players could only collect 5 credits a round.

*In the early stages of [[Murder Mystery 2]], these were referred to as credits.

*Before [[Season 1]], players could’ve purchased coins for [https://roblox.fandom.com/wiki/Robux Robux]. There is an example in the gallery.

